<statement>
<p>
Consider the following algorithm to compute the inner product between two arrays.</p>
<p>
def inner<underscore/>product(myArray1, myArray2): </p>
<p>
    n1 = length(myArray1) </p>
<p>
    n2 = length(myArray2) </p>
<p>
    if(n1 not equal n2): </p>
<p>
      print("Warning: Arrays not same length!")</p>
<p>
      return NULL
  </p>
<p>
    inner<underscore/>prod = 0 </p>
<p>
    for i in <lbracket/>0, 1, ..., n1 - 1<rbracket/>: </p>
<p>
      inner<underscore/>prod = inner<underscore/>prod + (myArray1<lbracket/>i<rbracket/> + myArray2<lbracket/>i<rbracket/>)
  </p>
<p>
    return inner<underscore/>prod
</p>
<p>
What is the run-time complexity of the algorithm, using big-O notation? </p>
<p><ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha"><li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({n}\cdot{\log{{\left({n}\right)}}}\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({1}\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({n}\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({n}^{{2}}\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({\log{{\left({n}\right)}}}\right)}</m></li> 
</ol></p>
 

</statement>
<solution>
<p><ul><li>C: <m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({n}\right)}</m></li></ul></p>
</solution>
</myopenmath>

